RETIRED — DO NOT INSTALL THIS FILE AS AN ORDER-STATUS ADDITIONAL SCRIPT.

The former example was unsafe because it:

1. treated every Shopify SKU as a GTIN even though a SKU is not evidence of a
   GTIN; and
2. invented an estimated delivery date by adding 14 days to the order date.

Google Customer Reviews may be rendered only by a checkout/order-status
integration that receives all required values from trusted order data. The
`estimated_delivery_date` must be an actual order-level estimate backed by the
selected product, processing path, destination, and carrier service. It must
not be calculated from a universal offset. Omit `products` unless each supplied
identifier is a verified GTIN for that exact line item. If a required value is
missing or invalid, skip the survey opt-in instead of supplying a fallback.

Any future implementation must also follow Shopify's current consent-aware
customer-privacy and pixel controls and must be reviewed against the visible
LuxeMia Privacy and Review policies before deployment.
